WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.650
Supernatural's Sam and Dean Winchester, played
by Jared Padalecki and Jensen Ackles, battled

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:10.960
legions of monsters for 15 seasons alongside
countless guest stars. Some left until their

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.780
characters returned to life, some left because
their characters were misunderstood, and some

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.220
left for other reasons. Find out why they
really said goodbye.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.130
Mark Sheppard played Crowley, the demonic
King of Hell, in seasons 5 through 12, and

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.880
he became an integral part of the show. He
secretly aided and openly antagonized the

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.440
Winchester brothers, acting as a friend or
foe whenever it was most convenient for his

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.930
purposes. But Sheppard felt that his character
deserved a better send-off from the show than

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:43.950
the way his final exit was written, in which
he sacrificed himself on an angel's blade.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.079
In a fan Q&amp;A, he expressed his disappointment,
saying,

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:51.210
"Once they decided they needed to do something
different [with the direction of the show],

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.800
they tried to get rid of me without telling
me that they were going to get rid of me.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.870
[...] I'd gone from being the smartest character
on the show to being the dumbest character

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.829
on the show in two seasons. They ran out of
what to do."

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:07.240
"No one in the history of torture's been tortured
with torture like the torture you'll be tortured

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.240
with…"

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.890
Needless to say, Sheppard did not part company
with the show on the best of terms.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:17.850
DJ Qualls joined Supernatural in season seven
as demon hunter Garth Fitzgerald, who preferred

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.869
working alone but was occasionally willing
to team up with the Winchesters. He later

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:27.150
underwent an intense transformation when he
became a werewolf.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:31.720
Qualls was very appreciative of the fans’
enthusiastic support, and said he had loved

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.830
working on Supernatural, but there was simply
no room in his schedule to return to the show.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:40.371
He told TVGuide,
"I'm so busy right now. [...] I'm on a couple

00:01:40.371 --> 00:01:43.810
different shows, and I have two films lined
up after this."

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:48.869
He regretted having let the Supernatural fandom
down, and promised to make time for the show,

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:53.159
eventually returning for guest spots in seasons
14 and 15.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:58.119
Katie Cassidy was the first actress on the
show to play Ruby, a demon who almost tore

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:02.820
the Winchester brothers' close relationship
apart. Cassidy said she felt that leaving

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:07.300
Supernatural was heartbreaking. Why did she
exit, despite loving her time on the show

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.789
so much?
According to series creator Eric Kripke, the

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:15.260
production company could no longer afford
to keep her on the payroll. But Cassidy offered

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.450
a slightly different explanation.
She told TVGuide,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.700
"Warner Bros. wasn't exactly sure what they
were going to be doing with my character,

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.310
and I had the option to stay or leave. [...] When
Harper's Island came about, I was really into

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.540
it, so I asked them to let me go. Luckily,
they did."

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.599
When Genevieve Cortese joined the cast of
Supernatural in season four to take over the

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:41.760
role of the demon Ruby, she didn't expect
that it would completely change her life.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.680
But Ruby’s scandalous on-screen relationship
with Sam Winchester blossomed into Genevieve’s

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.200
real-life romance with Jared Padalecki, who
admitted that he waited about four months

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.319
before asking her on a date. His patience
paid off in a big way: They were married not

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:01.940
long after the fourth season wrapped, and
she became Genevieve Padalecki.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:07.940
In 2012, Genevieve gave birth to the couple's
first child, a son named Thomas, and then

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:14.290
their children Austin and Odette arrived soon
after in 2013 and 2017. Padalecki has focused

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.170
on family since then, largely retiring from
acting, but did return to Supernatural for

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.940
a guest spot in the final season.
Jeffrey Dean Morgan was an original cast member

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.110
on Supernatural. He played Sam and Dean's
father John Winchester, who became a demon

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:33.459
hunter after his wife -- Sam and Dean’s
mother -- was killed by a demon. Given how

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:38.099
important he was in the brothers’ lives,
having sent them down their path, it’s surprising

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:42.519
he doesn't appear much past season three.
Although the showrunners had wanted to keep

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:47.250
him on and feature him more after season 2,
Morgan’s busy schedule left them with no

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.239
choice.
Writer Sera Gamble told Digital Spy,

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:54.760
"We would love to have him back, but he's
really busy. He's turned into a huge star

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.970
over here! We got to use his voice for an
episode at the end of last season, so there's

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.310
always a chance. We would love to bring back
the character if our schedules ever lined

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:05.810
up, but I don't think anyone should hold their
breath."

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:10.410
Thankfully, Morgan was able to return for
several guest spots as John in later seasons

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.939
of the show.
Alona Tal became part of the Supernatural

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:19.880
cast in season two as Jo Harvelle, whose mother
Ellen was a friend of the Winchesters’ dad.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.881
Jo teamed up with them to hunt demons until
her death, and appeared as a ghost in season

00:04:23.881 --> 00:04:27.860
seven, then never returned again.
Tal said that she would have embraced the

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.281
opportunity to appear on Supernatural again
as Jo, but she worried that the show’s new

00:04:32.281 --> 00:04:37.020
leadership didn't seem to fully understand
what she and Samantha Ferris, who had played

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.820
her mother, had brought to the table.
She told MEA Worldwide,

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.060
"I think what happened was that when Samantha
and I were part of the show, there were different

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.330
heads of creative. But the people [running
things] there have changed and I don't think

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:53.910
they know us very well or know our characters."
She also stated that she hoped to appear in

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.340
the series’ final season, but it didn't
pan out.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:02.389
Julian Richings played Death himself, also
known as the Grim Reaper or the Pale Horseman,

00:05:02.389 --> 00:05:07.580
on Supernatural. His appearances were rare
but unforgettable, especially considering

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:12.570
Death’s weakness for fattening food — he
just couldn't resist eating a meal at a diner.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:17.000
Richings made his final appearance as Death
in season 10, and in the following seasons

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.020
Lisa Berry took over the role. By the time
his last episode had come around, Richings

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:27.330
had already taken on a new recurring role
as the shadowy Benjamin Kertland on Orphan

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.070
Black, and it was the perfect time to step
away. Richings always seems to have a full

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:37.860
schedule, and since then, he's landed roles
on series including 12 Monkeys and Doom Patrol.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:43.690
Richard Speight Jr. played the archangel Gabriel,
disguised as the trickster Loki. Though always

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:48.480
mischievous, Gabriel eventually sided with
the Winchesters. Gabriel met his end in season

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:53.780
13 — but as it turned out, Speight himself
never really left Supernatural at all.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:58.650
In addition to acting, Speight left his mark
by directing several episodes of the series,

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:04.210
including some in the final season. He was
behind the camera for "Proverbs 17:3," "Our

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.449
Father, Who Aren't in Heaven," and "Galaxy
Brain."

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:13.490
Kurt Fuller appeared on Supernatural as the
villainous angel Zachariah. Fuller embraced

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:18.571
the chance to play an unsaintly bad guy and
ended up really enjoying it — in fact, he

00:06:18.571 --> 00:06:23.380
felt a little guilty about it! Admitting to
himself he needed a change, Fuller jumped

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:28.800
at the opportunity to join the situation comedy
Better With You, which he described. as "a

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.750
welcome relief" after his time on Supernatural.
He told Staying In,

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:37.060
"Making people laugh rather than making people
bleed is much more fun. And I feel better

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.419
about it. This is definitely better for my
soul."

00:06:40.419 --> 00:06:45.240
Carrie Anne Fleming appeared on Supernatural
as Karen Singer, wife of supporting character

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:49.900
Bobby Singer. She had been possessed by a
demon and then killed by her husband Bobby,

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.330
who didn't understand the paranormal nature
of what had happened to her.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:57.250
Fleming’s first guest appearance on the
show was marred by personal troubles, as she

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:02.160
struggled with postpartum depression at the
time. Sadly, she was also preparing to leave

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.319
her marriage.
Fleming would later joke to fans that "white

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:09.260
clown makeup and no sleep" was all it took
to make her look like a genuine zombie. But

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.889
at the time, she was so deeply troubled she
could barely get through a day on set.

00:07:13.889 --> 00:07:17.540
She told Times Colonist,
"I was having trouble being happy. [...] I

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:23.250
had trouble memorizing dialogue and communicating."
She did return to Supernatural in season seven,

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.780
which was hopefully a better experience.
Fans of Supernatural know Rick Worthy as the

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:34.630
Alpha Vampire, the very first member of the
vampire species. But when Worthy first auditioned,

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:39.180
he had wanted to play a much more prominent
and longer-term role: Crowley!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.500
He told Digital Spy,
"I really wanted to be on the show, and I

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.550
had auditioned probably five or six times
before. [...] I auditioned for the role of

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:51.500
Crowley, which I thought was a great role,
and was devastated, just devastated [when

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:55.039
I didn't get it]."
Unfortunately, because Worthy wasn't chosen

00:07:55.039 --> 00:07:59.740
for a major role, he couldn't stay on Supernatural
as long as he’d really wanted. He went on

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:03.240
to other roles including the strict Dean Fogg
on The Magicians.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:14.110
"Now, when we "freaks" die... where do we
go? Not heaven, not hell. So?"

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:18.720
